- op: discuss  # 2910
  at: '2026-08-09T23:09:08Z'  # 2910
  by: agent  # 2910
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 2910
  clock: 7  # 2910
  nonce: '2910'  # 2910
  message: "POPULATION MOVED, ITEM UNCHANGED (PR #254). This item's residual is that a bare\n`external` placeholder names no module, so a repo reaching I/O ONLY through untyped\nreceivers still confirms. PR #254 types constructor-ROOT receivers, which converts 260\npreviously-untyped call edges into catalogue-adjudicable ones across the 7-repo cohort\n(pretix / sqlalchemy / mitmproxy / poetry / pyright / meson / kserve).\n\nThat NARROWS the exposure without closing it, and the narrowing is small against the\npopulation: ~27,085 of 27,354 call-result-root sites in the same cohort still have\nreceivers of genuinely unknown type. Those deliberately emit no edge at all (PR #231\nmeasured that emitting an untyped edge moves zero findings).\n\nWHAT I DID NOT MEASURE, said plainly rather than implied: I did not re-run verify-claims\non those repos to see whether any verdict moved from confirmed to inconclusive or back.\nSo this entry records an input change, NOT a verdict change, and is not closure\nevidence. Status stays violated and the pinned test still passes."  # 2910
- op: discuss  # 2417
  at: '2026-08-11T04:56:51Z'  # 2417
  by: agent  # 2417
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 2417
  clock: 8  # 2417
  nonce: '2417'  # 2417
  message: "PREMISE RE-VERIFIED, RESIDUAL IS LIVE, AND THE OBVIOUS NEXT FIX IS REFUTED.\n\n1) The filed repro no longer false-confirms — PR #251 holds. poetry/src/poetry today: CONTROL-FSREAD violated (48 chains, so the run works), NET and DB both INCONCLUSIVE naming 59 uncovered modules. Re-ran the item's own repro rather than trusting a proxy.\n\n2) THE RESIDUAL REPRODUCES, and now has a durable fixture. A repo whose egress leaves only through an untyped receiver:\n     def upload(session, url, payload): return session.post(url, data=payload)\n   with a catalogued open() alongside as control. Result: CONTROL-FSREAD violated (2 chains) and NET **confirmed** — 'No net_send chains found'. That is the bucket-A failure verbatim: confirmed when the tool did not look.\n\n3) THE PROPOSED FINER SIGNAL IS DEAD. cli.py's docstring names the fix shape as 'resolution finer than any' — match an untyped call's METHOD NAME against catalogued method-kind primitives for the boundary under claim. Measured on poetry and kserve plus the fixture:\n     poetry  2,241 untyped-receiver edges: EVERY boundary would downgrade (db_read 234, ipc_recv 160, fs_read 93, fs_write 67, db_write 40, net_send 37, net_recv 35, ipc_send 1)\n     kserve  3,370 untyped edges: likewise EVERY boundary downgrades\n     fixture net_send would stay CONFIRMABLE (0 matching edges) while db_read and ipc_recv downgrade on an unrelated dict .get\n   So it blanket-downgrades on real repos — the same outcome already rejected — AND it is anti-correlated with the truth on the one case where the answer is known. The catalogued names are close/get/write/send/read/all/filter/update/save, i.e. the most common method names in Python, and 'post' is not a catalogued method name at all. DO NOT BUILD IT.\n\n4) WHAT IS ACTUALLY UNDERNEATH, filed as INV-fotav: requests, httpx and urllib3 have ZERO rows in the python catalogue. python.yaml's header asserts third-party libraries 'are detected transitively — they ultimately call these primitives', which is false in the normal case because hypergumbo analyzes the repo and not site-packages. Fixture: import requests; requests.post(url, data={'s': secret}) -> 0 net_send chains, with env_read and fs_read controls both firing. Corpus floor ~1,728 requests call sites.\n\nThis item stays violated. Its closure still runs through receiver typing (INV-linub L3) for the param-typed shape, but INV-fotav is the larger and cheaper half and closes both sides of the inconclusive/recall tension at once."  # 2417
- op: discuss  # e49b
