  nonce: e49b  # e49b
  message: "INV-fotav merged (dev 0a18354c50): the boundary arm now takes project-local overlays, so a user CAN make third-party egress visible instead of only getting 'inconclusive' on it. That closes the recall half of this item's tension. The residual pinned here is untouched — a receiver arriving as a bare function parameter still names no module, so the param-typed shape (def upload(session, ...): session.post(...)) still confirms. That remains receiver typing (INV-linub L3 / INV-dulum), not a gate."  # e49b
- op: discuss  # 6214
  at: '2026-08-11T17:51:21Z'  # 6214
  by: agent  # 6214
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 6214
  clock: 10  # 6214
  nonce: '6214'  # 6214
  message: "PREMISE RE-VERIFIED AND THE RESIDUAL IS NOW EXACTLY CHARACTERISED, with a two-arm\ncontrol rather than a single failing fixture.\n\nFIXTURE (stdlib only, so no overlay is involved and nothing depends on INV-fotav):\n\n    def control_fsread(p):\n        with open(p) as fh: return fh.read()\n\n    def send_unannotated(sock, payload):        # the residual\n        return sock.sendall(payload)\n\n    def send_annotated(sock: socket.socket, payload):\n        return sock.sendall(payload)\n\nRESULT, both arms:\n  BOTH functions present   -> CONTROL-FSREAD violated (2 chains); NET-SEND violated,\n                              1 net_send chain. So exactly ONE of the two shapes is seen.\n  ONLY the unannotated one -> CONTROL-FSREAD violated (2 chains); NET-SEND **CONFIRMED**,\n                              \"No net_send chains found.\"\n\nThat is the bucket-A failure verbatim -- confirmed when the tool did not look -- and the\ncontrol fires in both arms, so the null is not a broken run.\n\nSO THE RESIDUAL IS NARROWER THAN THIS ITEM'S TEXT SUGGESTS. An ANNOTATED parameter\nreceiver already works: _external_param_types (py.py) reads\n`func_node.args.args + kwonlyargs`, resolves `_annotation_module_hint`, and its own\ndocstring records the sizing -- of 95,245 method-call edges carrying the `external`\nplaceholder across six repos, 4,160 have a receiver with a resolvable annotation and 63\nreach the catalogue. What remains is precisely the UNANNOTATED parameter, where the\nfunction body contains no information to type the receiver from.\n\nTHE ONLY SOUND FIX IS INTERPROCEDURAL, and it should be sized before it is built:\npropagate the ARGUMENT type at each call site to the parameter (`s = socket.socket()`\nthen `send_unannotated(s, ...)`), typing a parameter only when every observed call site\nagrees on one type. Neither of this item's two previously-proposed fixes survives -- the\nmethod-name gate was measured anti-correlated with the truth and is recorded DO NOT\nBUILD, and annotation reading is already shipped.\n\nWHY IT IS NOT BEING BUILT IN THIS PASS, stated rather than implied. Measurement 0001\n(docs/measurements/0001-taint-flow-precision.md) puts taint-flow precision at ~41%\npopulation-weighted on six real repositories, and this is a RECALL fix that lands into\nthat reporting layer. The pre-registered consequence of the <50% band is that recall work\nwaits on the precision mechanisms being understood. The sizing this needs -- how many\n`external`-placeholder receivers are unannotated parameters whose call sites agree on one\ncatalogued type -- is a corpus measurement in its own right and is the honest next step.\n\nSTATUS UNCHANGED: violated. The repro above is the one to re-run."  # 6214
- op: discuss  # 1fa2
  at: '2026-08-17T22:03:47Z'  # 1fa2
  by: agent  # 1fa2
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 1fa2
  clock: 11  # 1fa2
  nonce: 1fa2  # 1fa2
  message: "P0/P1 SWEEP 2026-08-17, dev 11a240f83d. Every claim below was re-derived against the current tree, not re-read off this thread.\n\nTHE FILED REPRO NO LONGER REPRODUCES. Re-run live at dev 11a240f83d on the unmodified upstream repo this item names, with its own control:\n\n    hypergumbo verify-claims ~/ALL_REPOS/curriculum_repos/poetry/src/poetry --claims <fs_read + net_send, must_not_exist>\n\n      x [CONTROL-FSREAD]  violated, 72 fs_read chains   <- the run WORKED\n      ? [NET]             INCONCLUSIVE                  <- was 'confirmed'\n\nSo the headline defect -- a clean verdict reported as confirmed when the tool could not adjudicate the modules involved -- is not demonstrable on this item's own repro any more.\n\nBUT NOTE WHICH GATE FIRED, because it is not the one this item built. The inconclusive reason given is the OPAQUE-LAUNCH gate: 'the analysis launches an external program at 5 call site(s) (os.execvpe, subprocess.Popen, subprocess.check_call, subprocess.check_output, subprocess.run)'. Not the uncatalogued-module coverage gate from PR #251. poetry now trips a different, earlier gate, so it has stopped being a discriminating repro for THIS item's residual.\n\nSTATUS UNCHANGED: violated. The residual is unaffected and is pinned by test_untyped_receiver_population_is_the_disclosed_residual -- a repo whose I/O is reached ONLY through untyped 'external' receivers still confirms. What is now owed is a repro that ISOLATES that residual: a fixture or repo with an untyped-receiver boundary and no opaque launch. Until then this item has a live defect and no live repro, which is the shape that gets items falsely closed.\n\nTITLE CORRECTED to stop advertising the poetry repro as current."  # 1fa2
