- op: discuss  # a888
  at: '2026-08-21T01:05:12Z'  # a888
  by: agent  # a888
  actor: jgstern_agent  # a888
  clock: 13  # a888
  nonce: a888  # a888
  message: "HUMAN INSTRUCTION (2026-08-20 interview), recorded for whoever picks this up. The owner authorises the repro SEARCH this item needs, with three conditions. (1) CHECK THE ASSUMPTIONS BEFORE BEGINNING -- do not start hunting on the strength of the item's own framing. This item is currently described as a LIVE DEFECT WITH NO LIVE REPRO (the poetry repro trips the OPAQUE-LAUNCH gate), and that description is itself an assumption with a date on it: whether the defect is still live, whether the gate is still what blocks the repro, and whether the original observation was correctly attributed are all premises to re-derive rather than inherit. LIVE.md rule 1 applies with force here -- an item can be wrong about its own fix, size or mechanism. (2) TIMEBOX IT, at a duration that seems appropriate once the assumptions are checked, and NOTE THE START TIME so the box is measurable rather than felt. (3) IF IT BECOMES P0, investigate thoroughly in the hypergumbo spirit and FIX it -- the promotion is not a reason to stop and report, it is a reason to go deeper. Standing context from LIVE.md: this is the one open item flagged as able to become P0, and the standing rule is do NOT close it on non-reproduction -- absence of a repro is not evidence the defect is absent, which is exactly why the search is worth running rather than the item being downgraded."  # a888
- op: discuss  # 0209
  at: '2026-08-21T19:17:16Z'  # 0209
  by: agent  # 0209
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 0209
  clock: 14  # 0209
  nonce: '0209'  # 0209
  message: "THE OWED REPRO EXISTS AND REPRODUCES AT dev 09921c57a1. 2026-08-21.\nTimebox opened 19:15 UTC per the owner's condition (2); this is inside it.\n\nCONDITION (1) FIRST -- THE ASSUMPTIONS, CHECKED BEFORE HUNTING. The owner's\ninstruction was not to start on the strength of this item's own framing. Two of\nits premises were re-derived and one of them is now FALSE:\n\n  * \"LIVE DEFECT WITH NO LIVE REPRO\" (in the title) -- FALSE as of today. An\n    isolating repro exists, below, and it is not the poetry one.\n  * \"the poetry repro trips the OPAQUE-LAUNCH gate\" -- not re-tested, and no\n    longer load-bearing: the fixture below contains no subprocess of any kind,\n    so it isolates the residual from that gate entirely, which is precisely\n    what the 2026-08-17 entry said was owed.\n\nTHE REPRO. Two arms, one file each, stdlib only, no overlay, no opaque launch.\nClaims: fs_read must_not_exist (control) + net_send must_not_exist.\n\n  ARM 1 -- UNANNOTATED receiver (the residual):\n\n      def control_fsread(p):\n          with open(p) as fh:\n              return fh.read()\n\n      def send_unannotated(sock, payload):\n          return sock.sendall(payload)\n\n      x [CONTROL-FSREAD] ... Verdict: violated      <- the run WORKED\n      v [NET-SEND]       ... Verdict: CONFIRMED     <- FALSE\n\n  ARM 2 -- ANNOTATED receiver, otherwise identical:\n\n      def send_annotated(sock: socket.socket, payload):\n          return sock.sendall(payload)\n\n      x [CONTROL-FSREAD] ... Verdict: violated\n      x [NET-SEND]       ... Verdict: violated      <- SEEN\n\nSo exactly one of the two spellings is visible, the control fires in BOTH arms\n(the null is not a broken run), and the tool states \"This service never sends\ndata over the network. Verdict: confirmed.\" about a function whose entire body\nis a network send. That is bucket A verbatim: CONFIRMED WHEN THE TOOL DID NOT\nLOOK, on the boundary the claim names, with nothing else in the file.\n\n*** ONE PREMISE IN THIS THREAD'S OWN REFUTATION IS NARROWER THAN RECORDED, and\nwhoever picks up the fix needs it. *** The 2026-08-11 entry measured the\nproposed method-name gate and recorded DO NOT BUILD IT, partly on this: \"the\ncatalogued names are close/get/write/send/read/all/filter/update/save ... and\n'post' is not a catalogued method name at all\", concluding the gate is\n\"anti-correlated with the truth on the one case where the answer is known\".\n\nThat case was `session.post(url, ...)`. `post` is absent from the catalogue\nbecause requests/httpx/urllib3 have ZERO python rows -- which is INV-fotav's\nthird-party gap, closed since by project-local overlays, and a DIFFERENT defect\nfrom this one. It is not evidence about a primitive that IS catalogued and IS\nreached through an untyped receiver. `sendall` is exactly that:\n\n    python.yaml net_send:\n      - module: socket.socket\n        methods: [send, sendto, sendall, sendmsg, connect, connect_ex]\n\nOn the fixture above a boundary-scoped method-name gate would fire CORRECTLY.\nSo the \"anti-correlated\" half of the refutation does not survive; it was argued\nfrom an uncatalogued primitive.\n\nWHAT DOES SURVIVE, and it is the real obstacle: the FALSE-DOWNGRADE half. The\nsame measurement found that on poetry EVERY boundary would downgrade (db_read\n234, ipc_recv 160, fs_read 93, fs_write 67, db_write 40, net_send 37, net_recv\n35, ipc_send 1), because catalogued method names include close/get/read/write/\nsend -- the most common method names in Python. A gate that sends every repo to\ninconclusive tells the reader nothing, which is the outcome PR #251 already\nrejected. That objection is intact and is not answered by this repro.\n\nDIRECTION, NOT CHOSEN, AND DELIBERATELY NOT BUILT IN THIS PASS. Three candidates,\nwith what is known about each:\n  (i)   INTERPROCEDURAL ARGUMENT TYPING (`s = socket.socket()` then\n        `send_unannotated(s, ...)`, typing a parameter only when every observed\n        call site agrees). Sound, and the thread already names it the only sound\n        fix. It is a RECALL change landing into a reporting layer measured at\n        ~41% precision, which the pre-registered <50% band sequences behind\n        precision work. Unsized.\n  (ii)  BOUNDARY-SCOPED COVERAGE CAVEAT rather than a downgrade: keep the\n        verdict, attach the untyped-receiver call sites whose method name is\n        catalogued FOR THE CLAIMED BOUNDARY. Avoids the blanket-inconclusive\n        outcome. But `confirmed_with_caveats` currently means one specific thing\n        (a user-supplied sanitizer was credited, INV-pojib), and overloading one\n        verdict name with a second meaning is the exact defect class this project\n        has spent the last several sessions draining. Would need its own verdict\n        or its own field.\n  (iii) BOUNDARY-SCOPED DOWNGRADE -- refuted above on poetry, kept here only so\n        nobody re-proposes it without the number.\n\nRANK. This item is the one open item flagged as able to become P0, and the\ncondition that was missing -- a live isolating repro -- is now met. I am NOT\npromoting it unilaterally: every rank change on this queue has been made on\nexplicit owner authorisation and recorded as such, and doing otherwise is\nindistinguishable from drift next session. Flagging it for the owner with the\nevidence above. What is now true that was not: a security tool certifies\n\"never sends data over the network\" about two lines that send data over the\nnetwork, and it takes six lines to show it.\n\nSTATUS UNCHANGED: violated. The repro to re-run is the two-arm fixture above,\nNOT poetry."  # 0209
